WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.800
The original "John Wick" has stood the test of&nbsp;
time as one of the more perfect modern action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.920
movies. We've loved the premise since the first&nbsp;
time we heard it — man loses wife, man gets dog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.160
mobster kills dog, and man violently&nbsp;
gets his revenge on about ninety people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.000
The dog is avenged. A new dog is&nbsp;
acquired. All is right in the world.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.200
"That's crazy sh-t, man."

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.680
But then, the world expanded. "John Wick: Chapter&nbsp;
2" came along, furthering the story of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.120
vengeful assassin and ladling out more lore about&nbsp;
the circle of killers in which he used to run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.960
"Maybe," the film posits, "some people get&nbsp;
upset when their relatives get stomped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.320
the same way that John Wick got&nbsp;
upset about his stomped-up dog."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.640
Commence to more killing as John Wick fights&nbsp;
to survive the wave of shooters coming for him.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.080
John and his new dog go on the run,&nbsp;
with danger around every corner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.680
Common gets a knife stuck in his&nbsp;
torso! John Wick does Joker's trick!

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.560
"Ta-da!"

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.560
Truly, it doesn't get any better than&nbsp;
this… or so we thought. And then…

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.800
"I'm thinkin' I'm back!"

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.040
This is the world that viewers can expect&nbsp;
to walk into if they flip on "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.840
Chapter 3 — Parabellum," the threequel that's&nbsp;
making waves on Netflix in certain International&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.640
markets right this minute. Sorry Americans,&nbsp;
not on your Netflix, only other regions.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.360
It's a world of action. A world of adventure.&nbsp;
A world where the exchange rate on giant gold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.680
coins remains bamboozlingly inconsistent.&nbsp;
Like, you can use one to buy a gun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.840
but you can also use one to buy a gin and&nbsp;
tonic? Whatever, that's not the point.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.080
The movie picks up right where Chapter 2 left off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.720
so John Wick has a $14 million bounty on his&nbsp;
head. With an hour to leave the city and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.760
promise that he'll stomp any assassins that try&nbsp;
to take him out, our hero makes a hasty escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.920
taking a break to fight some guys in an&nbsp;
antique warehouse to keep things interesting.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:46.000
A jetsetting adventure is well underway,&nbsp;
and Wick takes off for Casablanca,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.320
searching for a higher-up from the High Table&nbsp;
— basically, he wants to speak to a manager.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.240
"I'd like to see the manager." "Of course."

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.680
Meanwhile, in New York,&nbsp;
change is the only constant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.880
and Wick's old buddies The Bowery King and Winston&nbsp;
are being forced out of their positions of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.200
on account of their having helped the protagonist.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.160
There's plenty of blood, lots of fights, a&nbsp;
horse-versus-motorcycle battle in heavy traffic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.240
and so on. Most importantly, thanks to&nbsp;
the addition of Halle Berry's Sofia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.200
the dogs finally get a chance to&nbsp;
do some stomping of their own.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.200
"Good to see you, too."

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.320
"I should shoot you in the head right now."
"I know."

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.200
Basically, if you're looking for a good time&nbsp;
at the movies and don't mind watching your hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:35.000
slaughtering roughly a hundred goons, "John Wick:&nbsp;
Chapter 3 — Parabellum" might just be your jam.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.240
"I gotta tell you, I've been looking&nbsp;
forward to meeting you for a long time."

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.520
It is a rare and beautiful thing to find a movie&nbsp;
about a guy who's great at shooting people that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.960
gets near-uniformly glowing reviews. "John Wick:&nbsp;
Chapter 3 — Parabellum" is that beautiful thing.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.000
With a Certified Fresh critics' rating of 89%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.040
on Rotten Tomatoes, the third movie in the saga&nbsp;
of John Wick is neck-and-neck with "Chapter 2"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.440
for the title of Best Reviewed Film in the&nbsp;
Franchise. The Chicago Tribune called it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.640
"the best of the three so far." The Guardian&nbsp;
extolled, quote, "fight sequences so balletic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.960
you might forget you're watching violence –&nbsp;
until Reeves sinks a knife into a man's eye."

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.720
Peter Travers of Rolling Stone, in a 4.5 out of&nbsp;
5 star review, told hesitant potential viewers,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.640
"You can wait around and hope for a bigger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.040
badder burst of action fireworks than 'John&nbsp;
Wick 3,' but you'd be kidding yourself."

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.520
All in all, "John Wick: Chapter 3" is everything&nbsp;
that fans could hope for in a blockbuster action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.760
sequel. It offers the same flavor of violence&nbsp;
being doled out in the first two films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.880
with a considered bump in intensity and&nbsp;
ambition from series director Chad Stahelski.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.600
The worst thing you can say about the&nbsp;
picture is that it ends with more of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.040
a question mark than a period, but&nbsp;
like everything else about the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.400
that's a choreographed move — "John Wick:&nbsp;
Chapter 4" is slated to hit theaters in 2022.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.560
"Nice to meet you, Mr. Wick."

